  - id: help-patchnotes
    group: 2
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6b53b25b61542e74a8bbebd556963be7, type: 3}
    title:
      key:
      bold: 0
      smallCaps: 0
      fallback: Patch Notes
      localized:
        m_TableReference:
          m_TableCollectionName: Wiki
        m_TableEntryReference:
          m_KeyId: 0
          m_Key: help.patchnotes.title
        m_FallbackState: 0
        m_WaitForCompletion: 0
        m_LocalVariables: []
    body:
      key:
      bold: 0
      smallCaps: 0
      fallback: "<b>Version 1.5.6</b>\n\n<b>Enemies and exploration</b>\n\u2022 Added goblins, snails, bats, flying skulls and Bombschrooms across the existing maps. Bats also appear in the Mines.\n\u2022 Rebalanced enemy appearances, health, damage and attack timing, with gentler early encounters in the Woods and fewer slimes dominating the River.\n\u2022 Bombschrooms approach before lighting a two-second fuse. Defeat them before the yellow bar fills. They drop Mushrooms, a new Cauldron ingredient.\n\u2022 Improved enemy movement and attacks, and corrected enemy sizes, health bars and projectile positions.\n\u2022 Added scenery trees so the Woods stays wooded as you clear tasks.\n\u2022 Reduced slime kill requirements to match the new enemy mix.\n\n<b>Slimes and statistics</b>\n\u2022 Slimes now have three entries: Small, Medium and Large. All five colours still appear in the world.\n\u2022 Kills across colours combine toward stat reveals and bonus damage for each size. Existing kills are preserved, and colour-specific quests still count the correct colour.\n\u2022 Expand a slime entry to see individual colour kill counts. Its main icon changes colour as you reveal more information.\n\u2022 General shows all discovered enemies and resources, with remaining discoveries grouped into numbered tiles.\n\u2022 Select an enemy or resource in General to open its detailed entry.\n\u2022 Portrait General now opens a map list. Undiscovered maps use hidden names and silhouette artwork.\n\u2022 Tidied discovery counts, lifetime statistics and recent-run information.\n\n<b>Quests and tutorials</b>\n\u2022 Find Ivan appears before your first trip to the Woods. That first trip gives you more time to reach him before enemies appear.\n\u2022 Your first Echo is now the Task Echo, with Combat Echo unlocked later. Orin explains how to use your first ability before you set off.\n\u2022 Combat Echoes move ahead to intercept enemies instead of trailing behind.\n\u2022 Updated quest dialogue and missing character portraits to fit the current story.\n\u2022 Town-building animations return you to your previous position in the quest list.\n\u2022 Completing Very Scary adds a scarecrow near Eva\u2019s house. Paths beside Fields upgrade with the rest of town.\n\u2022 Spooky is now Hollow. Eva\u2019s quest, A Spell for the Hollow, uses 100,000 Slime to transform part of town and open the way. Existing unlocks are preserved.\n\u2022 Fixed tutorial button states and hand placement in both orientations.\n\n<b>Settings and controls</b>\n\u2022 Added Dim Screen: keep the game running behind a dark screen that blocks accidental taps. Hold to return.\n\u2022 Added an optional Skip restart countdown setting.\n\u2022 Split Settings into Preferences, Gameplay and Save Files, with the version always visible.\n\u2022 Tap outside an open menu to close it. Tap the loot button again to close its panel.\n\u2022 Improved portrait spacing and back-button alignment.\n\n<b>Version 1.5.5</b>\n\n\u2022 Quests now show the character speaking, including an animated wisp for Orin.\n\u2022 Quests that need resources beyond your skill level appear under Locked. Each affected requirement shows the skill level you need.\n\u2022 When a quest changes the town, the camera shows what was built before returning to your quest list. You can skip the animation.\n\u2022 Flora and Tillman now give the quests to build and expand Fields. Plots you have already built stay unlocked.\n\u2022 Fields expansions unlock over a longer level curve, with higher wood costs for later plots.\n\u2022 Small trees are back. Small, medium and large trees unlock at Logging levels 1/15/38 for basic trees, 29/46/64 for Oak, 55/72/90 for Birch, and 81/98/107 for Spruce.\n\u2022 Existing orchard growth times and harvest XP are unchanged by the new Logging unlock levels.\n\u2022 Crop seed packs now have a flat 7% drop chance from their matching tasks.\n\u2022 In Fields, chop a timber tree at medium size or choose Keep growing for twice the resources and XP at full size. Auto grows trees to full size.\n\u2022 Fixed the order of the cucumber growth animation.\n\u2022 Added a Fields guide to the Library.\n\u2022 Task preferences put the skills most relevant to your current map first. Removed the extra filters and Favour heading; undiscovered tasks are shown as a count at the bottom.\n\u2022 Run graphs now have zoom controls. Bars above the displayed range are marked with an arrow, and you can still select them to see the full value.\n\u2022 Fixed the pinned quest list repeatedly changing width during landscape runs.\n\u2022 The Hub and Shop show a clock when the free shop bonus is ready. Quest stars now sit beside the menu text.\n\u2022 Removed the old Inventory pane from Quests. Resource links open the main Inventory.\n\u2022 Dad jokes stay on screen twice as long.\n\n<b>Version 1.5.4</b>\n\n\u2022 You can now change language on iOS and Android in Settings \u2192 Appearance.\n\u2022 New installs use the device language when supported. Saved language choices are kept.\n\u2022 Added Auto, Portrait and Landscape orientation options.\n\u2022 Added an option to keep the game view clear of camera cutouts.\n\u2022 Improved spacing in Settings.\n\u2022 Task preferences are grouped by skill, with a skill picker in portrait and up to three columns in landscape.\n\u2022 Task rows show a Favour toggle and, during runs, the current chance. Tap a task for its statistics, chance preview and next boost.\n\u2022 Undiscovered tasks are collapsed, and sorting sits at the top of the list.\n\u2022 Chests grant twice as much Looting XP.\n\u2022 Gold, Fire, Lirium and Copium chests now unlock at Looting levels 14, 20, 27 and 36.\n\u2022 Looting skill icons now use the matching Forge cores.\n\u2022 Lock individual foods to keep them out of Mix All. Your choices are remembered.\n\u2022 The Mix All preview excludes locked foods. Locked foods are dimmed, with clearer lock icons in both themes.\n\u2022 Shortened five fish names: Muck Muncher, Sir Splash, Bloopicus, Niblet and Flippy.\n\u2022 Construct and expand Fields directly without a separate quest hand-in. Resource costs and unlock requirements still apply.\n\u2022 A Fields icon appears on Town when a manual harvest is ready.\n\u2022 Opening another top menu closes the current window in landscape, matching portrait.\n\u2022 Moved the Forge\u2019s cost and result icons closer to Craft. Equip appears on the right when an item is ready.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge\u2019s Comparison heading and moved the stat rows up.\n\u2022 Stop for Vathrium stays hidden until you discover a Vathrium Core.\n\n<b>Version 1.5.3</b>\n\n\u2022 Added Compact to Quests to hide descriptions. Your choice is remembered.\n\u2022 The quest list uses columns in landscape when there\u2019s room. Requirements can sit side by side in both orientations.\n\u2022 Rewards now sit above requirements. Ready quests show Turn In beside their name and keep item costs visible without progress bars.\n\u2022 Quest pins sit closer to their names, with upright icons when pinned and slanted icons when unpinned.\n\u2022 Removed quest divider lines and adjusted spacing around headings and controls.\n\u2022 Fixed the shop showing \u201cStore unavailable\u201d on Android and Steam.\n\u2022 Steam prices now show currency symbols and the correct decimal places.\n\u2022 Fixed the adventure view turning black or shifting after rotating from landscape to portrait.\n\u2022 You can open Settings during tutorials and change appearance without losing your place.\n\u2022 Tutorial links are easier to read in light mode.\n\u2022 The Discord logo now matches the HUD text colour in both themes.\n\n<b>Version 1.5.2</b>\n\n\u2022 Your resource multiplier now survives deaths and repeat runs until you return to town, capped at 10\u00d7.\n\u2022 Food produces more stew, with bigger gains from higher-value ingredients.\n\u2022 Chicken, pork, mutton and steak produce 50% more stew.\n\u2022 Restored the Cauldron's Mix All button, added a stew preview, and made it remember the amount selected for each food.\n\u2022 Added Never stop to the Forge. It overrides the other stop rules and keeps crafting while materials are available.\n\u2022 The hero and Echoes now have the same chances to find seeds and saplings. Later varieties are rarer, with separate progressions for crops, fruit trees and timber trees.\n\u2022 Quests can only be turned in while in town.\n\u2022 Increased small text sizes throughout the game, especially in Quests.\n\u2022 Made quest reward icons consistent, including seed packs. Reduced oversized sapling icons and fixed gaps between Fields plots.\n\u2022 Reworked the run summary and live resource list with compact stats, return totals and resource bonuses. Landscape lists use two or three columns.\n\u2022 Added pocket watches that change tier with time away and chests that change tier as your resource total grows.\n\u2022 Improved portrait scrolling in Quests and resource lists so the bottom navigation stays accessible.\n\u2022 NPC meetings show names and keep health, stats, abilities and zoom controls visible while you wait.\n\u2022 Fixed tutorial controls being disabled when you need to press them. Menu shortcuts can advance their lesson, and pressing the active menu button can close the window when prompted.\n\u2022 Library now opens on Topics. Added a journal icon for patch notes.\n\u2022 Replaced Locked text on buff slots with padlock icons.\n\u2022 Shortened and corrected translations, and made material names consistent across the interface.\n\u2022 Tasting now starts only when you press Taste, and the first taste happens immediately. The rate starts at 2/s, increases to 10/s at Eva level 12 and reaches 100/s at level 42.\n\u2022 Updated the Cauldron layout in portrait and landscape. Collection details stay open on mobile and show card bonuses, collection bonuses and the next upgrade more clearly."
      localized:
        m_TableReference:
          m_TableCollectionName: Wiki
        m_TableEntryReference:
          m_KeyId: 0
          m_Key: help.patchnotes.body
        m_FallbackState: 0
        m_WaitForCompletion: 0
        m_LocalVariables: []
    details:
      key:
      bold: 0
      smallCaps: 0
      fallback: "<b>Previous updates</b>\n\n<b>Opening and progression</b>\n\u2022 Reworked the opening quests and NPC introductions.\n\u2022 Gill leads players to the River; Barkley leads them toward the Woods.\n\u2022 Gill rewards Old Boots. Ivan supplies materials and teaches players to forge and equip their first sword.\n\u2022 Menus and tutorials appear as their systems become relevant.\n\u2022 Quests can only be turned in while in town.\n\n<b>Interface</b>\n\u2022 Redesigned the Run Summary and added a compact in-run Stats panel.\n\u2022 Inventory now shows equipped items and equipment bonuses.\n\u2022 Added drag scrolling throughout the interface.\n\u2022 Rebuilt the Library with topic navigation, reference tables, and selectable icon explanations.\n\n<b>Gameplay and fixes</b>\n\u2022 Reduced task density on the first Farmlands adventure.\n\u2022 Farming tasks appear only in Farmlands.\n\u2022 Core and crystal tiers unlock through Combat levels.\n\u2022 Fixed enemy health-bar overlays and fishing animation issues.\n\u2022 Removed leaderboards.\n\n<b>Earlier patch notes</b>\n\n\u2022 Added For the Jam! and Gilliver's Travels.\n\u2022 Improved the introduction message.\n\u2022 Fixed level-up alerts showing lower values than expected.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge's Quality Equipped block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests show Ready to turn in instead of Complete.\n\u2022 Added a loading overlay when changing maps.\n\u2022 Added the Cauldron's Mix All button.\n\u2022 Updated the pathfinding package."
      localized:
        m_TableReference:
          m_TableCollectionName: Wiki
        m_TableEntryReference:
          m_KeyId: 0
          m_Key: help.patchnotes.details
        m_FallbackState: 0
        m_WaitForCompletion: 0
        m_LocalVariables: []
    illustrations: []
    referenceColumns: []
    referenceRows: []
    expanded: 0
    visibility: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
